        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: лопатка",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "лопатка (lopátka) — \"a shoulder blade; a small spade\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "У меня болит спина под левой лопаткой. U menyá bolít spiná pod lévoy lopátkoy. My back hurts under my left shoulder blade."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Also a small spade or a trowel: a diminutive of лопата — a spade."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "лопатка (lopátka) is a diminutive of лопата 'spade, shovel', which is inherited from Proto-Slavic lopata (EtymDB); the flat bone was named after the flat blade."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
