          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "EtymDB lists ладонь (ladón) without a source; it is usually traced to older долонь, from Proto-Slavic dolnь. Church Slavonic длань is the same word with -ла-: EtymDB traces длань through Church Slavonic to Proto-Slavic dolnь 'palm'."
            }
          ]
        },
